==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|wapentake}}, {{m|enm|wepentake}}, {{m|enm|wapentache}}, {{m|enm|wapentac}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wǣpenġetæc}}, from {{der|en|non|vápnatak}}, from {{m|non|vápn||weapon}} + {{m|non|taka||take}}, equivalent to {{af|en|weapon|take|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɒp.ən.teɪk/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[administrative]] [[subdivision]] in [[northern]] [[English]] [[counties]], developed under [[Norse]] influence, and corresponding to [[hundred]]s in the rest of England.

